From: Synkar <dev@synkar.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 20:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] brcmfmac: disable STA 4-way handshake / SAE offload

The BCM43752 firmware (FW 18.35.387.23.146) advertises the
NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_4WAY_HANDSHAKE_STA_PSK / STA_1X / SAE_OFFLOAD
extended features via the BRCMF_FEAT_FWSUP capability, signalling that
the firmware performs the 4-way handshake on its own.

On the AP6275P module (BCM43752) the firmware-supplicant (FWSUP) path
never completes the handshake against real APs: the firmware consumes
the EAPOL-Key frames internally but the connection never reaches the
authenticated/key-installed state from the host's perspective, so
wpa_supplicant loops on "Authentication timed out" (reason=3,
locally_generated=1) every ~10s and no data can flow. This reproduces
against every AP/SSID (WPA2-PSK, WPA3-SAE, multi-vendor).

Disable the STA-side FWSUP advertisement so the extended features are
not set: wpa_supplicant then runs the 4-way handshake (and SAE) in the
host over nl80211, which completes normally ([PTK=CCMP GTK=CCMP],
CTRL-EVENT-CONNECTED) and the link stays up. AP-mode offload (FWAUTH)
is left untouched since this device operates as a STA.

This is a workaround: the proper fix is to identify why the firmware
offload does not complete (suspected missing txcap_blob / NVRAM / FW
revision mismatch vs the vendor BSP where the offload works).

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -7727,7 +7727,7 @@
 		wiphy->flags |= WIPHY_FLAG_SUPPORTS_TDLS;
 	if (!ifp->drvr->settings->roamoff)
 		wiphy->flags |= WIPHY_FLAG_SUPPORTS_FW_ROAM;
-	if (brcmf_feat_is_enabled(ifp, BRCMF_FEAT_FWSUP)) {
+	if (0 && brcmf_feat_is_enabled(ifp, BRCMF_FEAT_FWSUP)) {
 		wiphy_ext_feature_set(wiphy,
 				      NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_4WAY_HANDSHAKE_STA_PSK);
 		wiphy_ext_feature_set(wiphy,
